\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 State Agency In Florida Tries to Steer  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Vote\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patricia Mazzei and Kate Zernike \par \uc2 786 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Florida agency charged with regulating health care providers, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics, publicly opposed a proposed ballot amendment that would guarantee \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a move that critics say is unethical and also, perhaps, a violation of state law.\par \par \uc2 ''Florida Is Protecting Life,'' reads the top of a website by the \uc2 Agency for Health Care Administration\uc2 . ''Don't let the fearmongers lie to you.''\par \par \uc2 The declaration, which was promoted on the social media platform X on Thursday by Jason Weida, the agency secretary, claims that the proposed amendment, known as Amendment 4, ''threatens women's safety.'' It lists several examples of what it says is the ''truth'' about the amendment's effects, using language typically employed by campaigns in favor of or against a ballot question. The website also includes data on political donations to the pro-amendment campaign.\par \par \uc2 The website seems to be an aggressive move by the administration of Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  against the ballot measure, which would allow abortions in Florida ''before viability,'' usually up to 24 weeks of pregnancy. Polls suggest that a majority of Florida voters favor the measure, though it would need more than 60 percent support to pass in November.\par \par \uc2 Mr. DeSantis, a Republican, has vowed to defeat the measure and has been raising money in a political committee against Amendment 4. But Governor DeSantis is an elected official. Mr. Weida, his appointed secretary, is not, nor are other agency employees.\par \par \uc2 ''You're not supposed to use your position in state government for electioneering,'' said State Representative Anna V. Eskamani, an Orlando Democrat, adding that the agency ''crossed a line.'' ''If you're going to do electioneering, you've got to provide a financial disclosure. There's all sorts of question marks here.''\par \par \uc2 Asked for comment on Thursday, the health agency defended the page as fulfilling its ''mission is to provide information and transparency to Floridians about the quality of care they receive.'' In his post on X, Mr. Weida said the page would ''combat the lies and disinformation surrounding Florida's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.''\par \par \uc2 In 2022, Governor DeSantis signed a law banning abortions at 15 weeks of pregnancy. And last year, Mr. DeSantis and Republican lawmakers further restricted the procedure, which as of May is now prohibited in Florida after six weeks.\par \par \uc2 The DeSantis administration has taken other steps to push back against Amendment 4. A state panel, largely appointed by Republicans, approved language in July for a financial impact statement that is required to accompany the amendment.\par \par \uc2 The statement says that Amendment 4 would result in ''significantly'' more abortions and fewer live births, and could force the state to pay high legal costs to resolve lawsuits that might result from it. It also says that an increase in abortions ''may negatively affect the growth of state and local revenues over time.''\par \par \uc2 Across the country, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have won on all seven ballot measures that have appeared since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade in June 2022, even in red states such as Kansas and Kentucky. In November, 10 states, including Florida, will have ballot amendments asking voters whether to establish a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 Republicans and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, openly fearing that the measures will pass, have worked aggressively to disqualify signatures on petitions seeking to establish the ballot measures, and make it harder for the measures to pass. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are suing to strike the measures certified for the ballots in Missouri, Nebraska and South Dakota.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, they have tried to shape the official language around the measures, and with Republicans in control of the process in many of the states, they have largely succeeded. The publicity pamphlets that Arizona will send to voters regarding the ballot measure refer to ''unborn human beings,'' a phrase that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups prefer to describe an embryo or fetus.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, a court in Missouri ruled that the ballot language that Secretary of State \uc2 Jay Ashcroft\uc2  had approved to appear on summaries at polling places was ''unfair, insufficient, inaccurate and misleading'' and ''gives voters the wrong idea of what the amendment will accomplish.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Ashcroft, a Republican fiercely opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had approved a summary saying that a ''yes'' vote would, among other things, ''enshrine the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time of pregnancy in the Missouri Constitution'' and ''prohibit any regulation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including regulations designed to protect women undergoing abortions.''\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups had sued, noting that, like those in almost every other state, the amendment would allow Missouri to regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after viability.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A9. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240907ek970000j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
