\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Religious Right Targeting I.V.F. As Allies Shift\b0\par\par\uc2 By Elizabeth Dias \par \uc2 1,388 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 August 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republicans may be backing away from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but these activists have a strategy, with or without Trump.\par \par \uc2 The pivot seems clear. The Republican Party of the post-Roe era is sidelining anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists. Project 2025, the conservative blueprint with innovative \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, has been disavowed by Donald Trump. And the new G.O.P. platform even promises to advance access to in vitro fertilization.\par \par \uc2 But as Mr. Trump distances himself from the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  revolution his own administration ushered in, a powerful battalion of conservative Christians has pushed ahead. In recent months, they have quietly laid the groundwork for their fight to restrict not only access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but also to I.V.F.\par \par \uc2 They are planting seeds for their ultimate goal of ending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from conception, both within the Republican Party and beyond it. They face a tough political battle since their positions are largely unpopular and do not reflect majority opinion, particularly on I.V.F.\par \par \uc2 As they see it, their challenge spans generations, not simply a single political cycle. And their approach -- including controlling regulatory language, state party platforms and the definition of when life begins -- reflects an incremental strategy similar to the one activists used for decades to eventually overturn Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 ''I expect there will be steps backwards as well as what we are working toward, which are long strikes forward,'' said R. Albert Mohler Jr., president of the Southern Baptist Theological Seminary in Louisville, Ky., who has been newly mobilizing evangelicals against I.V.F.\par \par \uc2 The fall of Roe itself was far from linear, he noted. ''It was nearly a half century of work, a half century of frustration, a half century of setbacks as well as advances,'' Mr. Mohler said. ''It will be a hard uphill climb, but that's what we are called to.''\par \par \uc2 Some of this groundwork is easy to notice. Mr. Mohler helped lead a successful campaign in June to get the \uc2 Southern Baptist Convention\uc2 , the country's largest Protestant denomination, to oppose the use of I.V.F. for the first time, even though the procedure is widely popular among evangelical families. The vote served to redirect the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversation within evangelical churches to fertility treatments, and to give ardent I.V.F. opponents a new data point to prove to Republican politicians that their key voters could support efforts against I.V.F.\par \par \uc2 Other change is happening more quietly. This year, several state Republican parties added new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  language to their own platforms, even if the national party went the opposite direction. Idaho's Republican Party added a five-word phrase -- ''the destruction of human embryos'' -- to a list of things it opposes, indicating a stand against common I.V.F. procedures. A similar line already existed in North Carolina's platform.\par \par \uc2 Texas Republicans added a line defining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as ''homicide,'' creating an argument for possible prosecutions for doctors who perform the procedure and women who undergo it. South Carolina added language that took aim at the Food and Drug Administration's approval of a common medication used in pregnancy terminations, including miscarriages: ''We oppose the F.D.A. and their efforts to make 'chemical abortions' easily obtainable and accessible.''\par \par \uc2 The national Republican platform removed a reference to ''children before birth.'' But the movement to advance ''fetal personhood'' -- granting embryos rights as persons through a novel reading of the 14th Amendment -- continues to press ahead.\par \par \uc2 Students for Life of America, a prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group, wants increased regulation of I.V.F. It is working to create a legal rationale for fetal personhood in forthcoming \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related bills in Congress and in the states. Its strategy follows a similar one, carefully planned by activists, that led to the Mississippi \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban's undoing of Roe.\par \par \uc2 Roe had blocked efforts to advance an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  argument about the 14th Amendment, said Kristi Hamrick, a longtime strategist for the group. ''But Roe is gone, and we are in a new legal environment, and so it makes sense that that becomes part of our conversation,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 There is also a new anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ''minority report,'' issued by a coalition of 19 Republican delegates to the convention, to emphasize their discontent with the party platform.\par \par \uc2 The delegates, led by \uc2 Tony Perkins\uc2 , the president of the conservative \uc2 Family Research Council\uc2 , stressed their goals of ''ending the exploitation of embryonic human beings, and above all recognizing the application of 14th Amendment protections to our developing offspring.''\par \par \uc2 Though their views did not make the main convention stage, they have an ideological ally in JD Vance, who has said he is ''100 percent pro-life.'' Even now as Mr. Vance, the vice-presidential candidate, defends Mr. Trump's backtracked positions, he has used the safety language common to anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, when discussing Mr. Trump's views on mifepristone, a widely available drug used in medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ''He just wants to make sure that drugs are safe and effective before they're out there in the market, and of course that doctors are properly controlling this stuff so that people don't get hurt,'' Mr. Vance said Sunday on \uc2 CBS\uc2 's ''Face the Nation.''\par \par \uc2 The American Association of Pro-Life OB-GYNs, one of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups that sued the F.D.A. to curtail distribution of mifepristone, currently does not have a position on I.V.F., but it is mapping out new guidance for the procedure. Although its case was recently rejected by the Supreme Court, the group started a lobbying wing in June to prepare for future advocacy campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Christina Francis, who leads the association, said the group was planning a report that would not take a position against I.V.F. Instead it would identify ''the gaps in our ethics surrounding I.V.F.,'' she said, and suggest some ''guardrails.'' That rhetoric -- ''ethics'' and ''guardrails'' -- reflects a similar strategy that was used to eventually achieve the Partial Birth \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ban Act.\par \par \uc2 Germany, Dr. Francis pointed out, limits I.V.F., and she suggested that I.V.F. procedures would ideally create one embryo, or for an older woman, possibly two.\par \par \uc2 ''You're definitely going to have the least number of ethical dilemmas if you are doing fresh transfer,'' without freezing embryos, she said. ''Even just having this discussion as a country, and as a profession honestly in medicine, is a good discussion to have.''\par \par \uc2 Kristen Ullman, president of the Eagle Forum, which was founded by the social conservative leader \uc2 Phyllis Schlafly\uc2 , said that her movement could ''absolutely'' move forward to regulate I.V.F., despite the ''disappointment'' of the G.O.P. position.\par \par \uc2 ''The platform, it's not legislation,'' she said. And while the new Republican platform is much shorter with fewer specifics on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related policy priorities, it has an upside, she added: ''You can be deliberately vague.''\par \par \uc2 In the past, rejection by the Republican Party has prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents to double down and find new ways to gain power. After \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  lost the 2012 presidential election, party leaders explicitly blamed anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists, saying their views were out of step with a liberalizing America. But activists pushed back and used an outsider, Mr. Trump, to leverage their power, embedding themselves in his administration and his remade Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  coalition knows that its ambitions would once again almost certainly be advanced by another Trump term, with government officials who share its goals and would be embedded in powerful positions.\par \par \uc2 For years before Roe was overturned, activists pursued policies at the edges, using reporting requirements and data gathering, to lay a foundation for their ultimate goals. Today, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists see ways to use these officials to chip away at access for the procedure and potentially fertility treatments through new regulations from federal agencies like the F.D.A., Health and Human Services, and the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ''What will happen in a Trump administration is all dependent on the people that are in the administration,'' Ms. Ullman said.\par \par \uc2 Frozen egg samples inside an I.V.F. facility. Christian conservative activists are laying the groundwork to restrict the procedure. (PHOTOGRAPH BY MICHAEL WYKE/ASSOCIATED PRESS) (A18) This article appeared in print on page A1, A18. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240815ek8f0003k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
