\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Hostility to  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Defined Vance's Rise but May Not Guide His Future\b0\par\par\uc2 By Lisa Lerer \par \uc2 983 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 13\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 As he joins Donald J. Trump's presidential ticket, Mr. Vance is seeking to play down, and in some cases rewrite, his views.\par \par \uc2 Throughout his brief political career, Senator J.D. Vance of Ohio has been an unapologetic opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a view driven by his Catholic faith and one he has cited as a driving force in his agenda.\par \par \uc2 He has supported a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, opposed exceptions for rape and incest, said he wanted to protect life ''from the date of conception'' and frequently described himself as ''100 percent pro-life.''\par \par \uc2 ''I think two wrongs don't make a right; at the end of day, we are talking about an unborn baby,'' he told an Ohio radio host in September 2021 before Roe v. Wade was overturned in part by three Supreme Court justices appointed by the man who named him to the Republicans' 2024 presidential ticket. ''It's not whether a woman should be forced to bring a child to term. It's whether a child should be allowed to live.''\par \par \uc2 In January 2023, Mr. Vance signed a letter asking the Justice Department to enforce the Comstock Act, a long-dormant law from 1873, to ban the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication. Such an action could significantly limit access to such medication, which accounts for a majority of abortions in the country.\par \par \uc2 ''While the use of chemical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs may be legal in some states, and federal law does not currently explicitly prohibit the use of such drugs, federal law does prohibit the mailing or shipping of such items,'' read the letter, which was signed by more than two dozen Republican lawmakers. ''Despite attempts to downplay this action, the 'mere mailing' of these items is expressly what the law has prohibited for nearly 150 years.''\par \par \uc2 Enforcing the Comstock Act is included in a plan released by a coalition that has been drawing up America First-style policy plans, nicknamed Project 2025 -- though the law is referred to only by the statute number. Mr. Vance has publicly praised those plans as containing ''some good ideas,'' even as former President Donald J. Trump has tried to distance himself from the effort.\par \par \uc2 Now, as he joins Mr. Trump's presidential ticket, Mr. Vance is seeking to play down -- and in some cases rewrite -- those views, saying he backs Mr. Trump's support for ''reasonable exceptions'' and for allowing states to decide their own limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ''My view is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the leader of the Republican Party, and his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are going to be the views that dominate this party and drive this party forward,'' Mr. Vance said on Monday in an interview on Fox News, after he was named to the ticket. ''You have to believe in reasonable exceptions because that's where the American people are. And you've got to let individual states make this decision.''\par \par \uc2 His current position is a clear softening for a candidate who once described staunch opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as one of the most crucial litmus tests for conservatives.\par \par \uc2 Since entering politics in 2022, with his run for a Senate seat in Ohio, Mr. Vance has cast himself as a fierce opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, supporting a Texas law that made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  functionally illegal in the state and that authorizes residents to enforce the ban. The 2021 law transformed Texas, criminalizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the Supreme Court overturned the right nationwide.\par \par \uc2 ''I think one of the most important issues for the conservative movement is the right to life,'' Mr. Vance told a crowd gathered for a campaign town-hall-style meeting in February 2022. ''If you're not willing to stand on that issue, I think it indicates your character is weak and you don't have the fortitude to actually serve the interest of our voters.''\par \par \uc2 He carried those beliefs into the Senate, where he has voted against protecting the right to fertility treatments like I.V.F. He has also opposed judicial nominees with a history of supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and legislation that expressed support for protecting access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance has urged Republicans to be not just anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  but ''pro-baby and pro-family and pro-people who are raising our families.''\par \par \uc2 He has cast Democrats as extreme on the issue, saying that the party supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until birth. Abortions so late in pregnancy are very rare, making up less than 1 percent of all procedures. Most Democrats say the issue should be left for women and their doctors to decide.\par \par \uc2 President Biden's campaign sees fresh opportunities in Mr. Vance's past statements. On Wednesday evening, it plans to release an advertisement featuring Hadley Duvall, a Kentucky \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights activist who says she was raped by her stepfather as a girl.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance is fluent in the language of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, attacking what followers often call the ''\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby'' and likening \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to American slavery.\par \par \uc2 ''There's something comparable between \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and slavery,'' Mr. Vance said, ''and that while the people who obviously suffer the most are those subjected to it, I think it has this morally distorting effect on the entire society.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance was so outspoken in his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views that he won a 100 percent rating from Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, a prominent anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  political organization.\par \par \uc2 ''J.D. Vance is an exceptional selection as President Trump's running mate,'' said Marjorie Dannenfelser, the president of the group, who praised his ''courage'' in ''exposing the Democrats' agenda of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for any reason.''\par \par \uc2 Senator J.D. Vance once asked the Justice Department to enforce the Comstock Act to ban the mailing of \uc2  medication. (PHOTOGRAPH BY ERIC LEE/THE NEW YORK TIMES) This article appeared in print on page A13. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240719ek7j0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
